#student examination eligibility system

Algorithm:

1. Start.
2. Enter the student's name.
3. Enter attendance percentage and internal marks.
4. Enter laboratory completion status and fee payment status.
5. Check whether attendance is at least 75% and internal marks are at least 20 out of 40.
6. Check whether the laboratory is completed and fees are paid.
7. If all conditions are satisfied, display Eligible; otherwise, display Not Eligible.
8. Stop.


Flowchart:

Start
Input student details
Check attendance ≥ 75% and internal marks ≥ 20
Lab completed and fees paid?
Yes to all
Eligible

No to any
Not Eligible

Display examination eligibility

Stop


code:

name = input("Enter student name: ")
attendance = float(input("Enter attendance percentage: "))
marks = float(input("Enter internal marks out of 40: "))
lab = input("Lab completed? (yes/no): ").lower()
fees = input("Fees paid? (yes/no): ").lower()

if not (0 <= attendance <= 100 and 0 <= marks <= 40):
    print("Invalid input")
elif (attendance >= 75 and marks >= 20
      and lab == "yes" and fees == "yes"):
    print("\nStudent Name:", name)
    print("Result: Eligible for final examination")
else:
    print("\nStudent Name:", name)
    print("Result: Not eligible for final examination")



